            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-59869",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml: js-yaml: Denial of Service via crafted YAML documents"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-59869\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: js-yaml\nFixed Version: 3.15.0, 4.3.0\nLink: [CVE-2026-59869](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869)\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-59869**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|js-yaml|3.15.0, 4.3.0|[CVE-2026-59869](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-59869)|\n\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 before 3.15.0 and from 4.0.0 before 4.3.0, js-yaml can spend quadratic CPU time parsing a document whose size grows only linearly when a chain of mappings uses merge keys where each mapping merges the previous one. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.0 and 4.3.0."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-84375",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml: js-yaml: Denial of Service vulnerability in YAML parsing"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 until 3.15.2 and 4.3.2, maxTotalMergeKeys in lib/js-yaml/loader.js and lib/loader.js does not count empty mapping sources while processing the merge key \u003c\u003c. An attacker can alias a large sequence of empty mappings into many merge targets, causing O(N * K) processing while totalMergeKeys remains unchanged and the configured resource limit is never reached. A relatively small YAML document can therefore cause prolonged CPU consumption in applications that parse untrusted YAML, and merge processing is enabled by default on these release lines. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.2 and 4.3.2."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-84375",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-84375\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: js-yaml\nFixed Version: 4.3.2, 3.15.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-84375](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-84375)\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 until 3.15.2 and 4.3.2, maxTotalMergeKeys in lib/js-yaml/loader.js and lib/loader.js does not count empty mapping sources while processing the merge key \u003c\u003c. An attacker can alias a large sequence of empty mappings into many merge targets, causing O(N * K) processing while totalMergeKeys remains unchanged and the configured resource limit is never reached. A relatively small YAML document can therefore cause prolonged CPU consumption in applications that parse untrusted YAML, and merge processing is enabled by default on these release lines. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.2 and 4.3.2.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-84375**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|js-yaml|4.3.2, 3.15.2|[CVE-2026-84375](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-84375)|\n\njs-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. From 3.0.0 until 3.15.2 and 4.3.2, maxTotalMergeKeys in lib/js-yaml/loader.js and lib/loader.js does not count empty mapping sources while processing the merge key \u003c\u003c. An attacker can alias a large sequence of empty mappings into many merge targets, causing O(N * K) processing while totalMergeKeys remains unchanged and the configured resource limit is never reached. A relatively small YAML document can therefore cause prolonged CPU consumption in applications that parse untrusted YAML, and merge processing is enabled by default on these release lines. This issue is fixed in versions 3.15.2 and 4.3.2."
              },
              "properties": {
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "7.5",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "HIGH"
                ]
              }
