              "id": "CVE-2025-64718",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml: js-yaml prototype pollution in merge"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "js-yaml is a JavaScript YAML parser and dumper. In js-yaml before 4.1.1 and 3.14.2, it's possible for an attacker to modify the prototype of the result of a parsed yaml document via prototype pollution (`__proto__`). All users who parse untrusted yaml documents may be impacted. The problem is patched in js-yaml 4.1.1 and 3.14.2. Users can protect against this kind of attack on the server by using `node --disable-proto=delete` or `deno` (in Deno, pollution protection is on by default)."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2025-64718",
              "help": {
