            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-5038",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "multer: Multer: Denial of Service via aborted or malformed multipart uploads"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Impact: multer versions 2.0.0-alpha.1 through 2.1.1 and 3.0.0-alpha.1 are vulnerable to a Denial of Service when using diskStorage. Aborted or malformed multipart uploads leave orphaned partial files on disk because the Readable.pipe() call does not propagate the stream destroy signal to \nthe underlying fs.WriteStream. An attacker can exhaust disk space by triggering many aborted uploads, with no application bug required.\n\nPatches: Users should upgrade to multer 2.2.0 (2.x line) or 3.0.0-alpha.2 (3.x prerelease). Both versions track in-flight write streams and clean them up on the abort path.\n\nWorkarounds: None."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5038",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-5038\nSeverity: MEDIUM\nPackage: multer\nFixed Version: 2.2.0, 3.0.0-alpha.2\nLink: [CVE-2026-5038](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5038)\nImpact: multer versions 2.0.0-alpha.1 through 2.1.1 and 3.0.0-alpha.1 are vulnerable to a Denial of Service when using diskStorage. Aborted or malformed multipart uploads leave orphaned partial files on disk because the Readable.pipe() call does not propagate the stream destroy signal to \nthe underlying fs.WriteStream. An attacker can exhaust disk space by triggering many aborted uploads, with no application bug required.\n\nPatches: Users should upgrade to multer 2.2.0 (2.x line) or 3.0.0-alpha.2 (3.x prerelease). Both versions track in-flight write streams and clean them up on the abort path.\n\nWorkarounds: None.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-5038**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|MEDIUM|multer|2.2.0, 3.0.0-alpha.2|[CVE-2026-5038](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2026-5038)|\n\nImpact: multer versions 2.0.0-alpha.1 through 2.1.1 and 3.0.0-alpha.1 are vulnerable to a Denial of Service when using diskStorage. Aborted or malformed multipart uploads leave orphaned partial files on disk because the Readable.pipe() call does not propagate the stream destroy signal to \nthe underlying fs.WriteStream. An attacker can exhaust disk space by triggering many aborted uploads, with no application bug required.\n\nPatches: Users should upgrade to multer 2.2.0 (2.x line) or 3.0.0-alpha.2 (3.x prerelease). Both versions track in-flight write streams and clean them up on the abort path.\n\nWorkarounds: None."
              },
